Explain photosynthesis simply}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af14\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1058\langfe2052\hich\af3\loch\ql\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f3\fs24\lang1058\kerning1\dbch\af12\langfe2052\loch\ql\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0\sb0\sa0{\rtlch\afs22\ab0 \ltrch\lang1033\hich\af9\loch\strike0\fs22\lang1033\ulnone\ulc0\b0\animtext0\f9\loch
Photosynthesis is the process where plants use sunlight, water, and carbon dioxide to make their own food and release oxygen. }
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af14\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1058\langfe2052\hich\af3\loch\ql\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f3\fs24\lang1058\kerning1\dbch\af12\langfe2052\loch\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0\sb0\sa0{\rtlch\afs22 \ltrch\hich\af9\loch\strike0\fs22\ulnone\ulc0\b\animtext0\f9\loch
What is Photosynthesis?}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af14\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1058\langfe2052\hich\af3\loch\ql\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f3\fs24\lang1058\kerning1\dbch\af12\langfe2052\loch\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0\sb0\sa12{\rtlch\afs22 \ltrch\hich\af9\loch\strike0\fs22\ulnone\ulc0\b0\animtext0\f9\loch
The word comes from Greek: "photo" means light, and "synthesis" means putting together. Plants act like tiny solar kitchens. They take raw ingredients from their environment and transform them into energy. }
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af14\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1058\langfe2052\hich\af3\loch\ql\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f3\fs24\lang1058\kerning1\dbch\af12\langfe2052\loch\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0\sb0\sa0{\rtlch\afs22 \ltrch\hich\af9\loch\strike0\fs22\ulnone\ulc0\b\animtext0\f9\loch
The Three Main Ingredients}
