\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af14\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1058\langfe2052\hich\af3\loch\ql\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f3\fs24\lang1058\kerning1\dbch\af12\langfe2052\loch\ql{\rtlch\afs32\ab \ltrch\lang1033\loch\fs32\lang1033\b\loch
Explain how gravity-speed work on time}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af14\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1058\langfe2052\hich\af3\loch\ql\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f3\fs24\lang1058\kerning1\dbch\af12\langfe2052\loch\ql\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0\sb0\sa0{\rtlch\afs22\ab0 \ltrch\lang1033\hich\af9\loch\strike0\fs22\lang1033\ulnone\ulc0\b0\animtext0\f9\loch
Gravity slows down the passage of time, an effect known as }{\rtlch\afs22\ab0 \ltrch\lang1033\hich\af9\loch\strike0\fs22\lang1033\ul\ulc0\b0\animtext0\f9\loch
gravitational time dilation}{\rtlch\afs22\ab0 \ltrch\lang1033\hich\af9\loch\strike0\fs22\lang1033\ulnone\ulc0\b0\animtext0\f9\loch
. }
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af14\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1058\langfe2052\hich\af3\loch\ql\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f3\fs24\lang1058\kerning1\dbch\af12\langfe2052\loch\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0\sb75\sa0{\rtlch\afs22\ab0 \ltrch\hich\af9\loch\strike0\fs22\ulnone\ulc0\b0\animtext0\f9\loch
How Gravity Affects Time}
\par \pard\plain \s22\rtlch\af14\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1058\langfe2052\hich\af3\loch\ql\sl276\slmult1\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa140\ltrpar\cf0\f3\fs24\lang1058\kerning1\dbch\af12\langfe2052\loch{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af6 \ltrch\hich\af6\loch\f6\dbch\af6 \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls3 \li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi-283\tx0\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi-283\sb0\sa0{\rtlch\afs22\ab0 \ltrch\hich\af9\loch\cs17\rtlch\ab \ltrch\loch\b\strike0\fs22\ulnone\ulc0\b0\animtext0\f9\loch
The Spacetime Fabric:}{\rtlch\afs22\ab0 \ltrch\hich\af9\loch\strike0\fs22\ulnone\ulc0\b0\animtext0\f9\loch
 Space and time are linked together in a single fabric called spacetime.}
\par \pard\plain \s22\rtlch\af14\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1058\langfe2052\hich\af3\loch\ql\sl276\slmult1\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa140\ltrpar\cf0\f3\fs24\lang1058\kerning1\dbch\af12\langfe2052\loch{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af6 \ltrch\hich\af6\loch\f6\dbch\af6 \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls3 \li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi-283\tx0\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi-283\sb0\sa0{\rtlch\afs22\ab0 \ltrch\hich\af9\loch\cs17\rtlch\ab \ltrch\loch\b\strike0\fs22\ulnone\ulc0\b0\animtext0\f9\loch
Mass Warps Spacetime:}{\rtlch\afs22\ab0 \ltrch\hich\af9\loch\strike0\fs22\ulnone\ulc0\b0\animtext0\f9\loch
 Heavy objects like stars and planets (including Earth) bend and curve this fabric.}
\par \pard\plain \s22\rtlch\af14\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1058\langfe2052\hich\af3\loch\ql\sl276\slmult1\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa140\ltrpar\cf0\f3\fs24\lang1058\kerning1\dbch\af12\langfe2052\loch{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af6 \ltrch\hich\af6\loch\f6\dbch\af6 \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls3 \li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi-283\tx0\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi-283\sb0\sa0{\rtlch\afs22\ab0 \ltrch\hich\af9\loch\cs17\rtlch\ab \ltrch\loch\b\strike0\fs22\ulnone\ulc0\b0\animtext0\f9\loch
Clocks Run Slower Near Mass:}{\rtlch\afs22\ab0 \ltrch\hich\af9\loch\strike0\fs22\ulnone\ulc0\b0\animtext0\f9\loch
 The closer you are to a heavy object (where gravity is strongest), the slower your clock ticks compared to someone far away in weaker gravity. }
\par \pard\plain \s22\rtlch\af14\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1058\langfe2052\hich\af3\loch\ql\sl276\slmult1\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa140\ltrpar\cf0\f3\fs24\lang1058\kerning1\dbch\af12\langfe2052\loch\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0\sb0\sa0{\rtlch\afs22\ab0 \ltrch\hich\af9\loch\strike0\fs22\ulnone\ulc0\b0\animtext0\f9\loch
Movement Through Spacetime}
\par \pard\plain \s22\rtlch\af14\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1058\langfe2052\hich\af3\loch\ql\sl276\slmult1\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa140\ltrpar\cf0\f3\fs24\lang1058\kerning1\dbch\af12\langfe2052\loch{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af6 \ltrch\hich\af6\loch\f6\dbch\af6 \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls4 \li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi-283\tx0\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi-283\sb0\sa0{\rtlch\afs22\ab0 \ltrch\hich\af9\loch\cs17\rtlch\ab \ltrch\loch\b\strike0\fs22\ulnone\ulc0\b0\animtext0\f9\loch
The Constant Speed of Light:}{\rtlch\afs22\ab0 \ltrch\hich\af9\loch\strike0\fs22\ulnone\ulc0\b0\animtext0\f9\loch
 Everything in the universe moves through spacetime at a single constant speed\uc2 \u8212\'81\'5cthe speed of light (\\(c\\)). \uc1 }
\par \pard\plain \s22\rtlch\af14\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1058\langfe2052\hich\af3\loch\ql\sl276\slmult1\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa140\ltrpar\cf0\f3\fs24\lang1058\kerning1\dbch\af12\langfe2052\loch{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af6 \ltrch\hich\af6\loch\f6\dbch\af6 \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls4 \li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi-283\tx0\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi-283\sb0\sa0{\rtlch\afs22\ab0 \ltrch\hich\af9\loch\cs17\rtlch\ab \ltrch\loch\b\strike0\fs22\ulnone\ulc0\b0\animtext0\f9\loch
Trading Space for Time:}{\rtlch\afs22\ab0 \ltrch\hich\af9\loch\strike0\fs22\ulnone\ulc0\b0\animtext0\f9\loch
 If you stay still in space, you travel through time at the maximum possible speed. If you move fast through space, or if gravity pulls on you, part of that movement budget shifts away from time. }
\par \pard\plain \s22\rtlch\af14\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1058\langfe2052\hich\af3\loch\ql\sl276\slmult1\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa140\ltrpar\cf0\f3\fs24\lang1058\kerning1\dbch\af12\langfe2052\loch{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af6 \ltrch\hich\af6\loch\f6\dbch\af6 \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls4 \li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi-283\tx0\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi-283\sb0\sa0{\rtlch\afs22\ab0 \ltrch\hich\af9\loch\cs17\rtlch\ab \ltrch\loch\b\strike0\fs22\ulnone\ulc0\b0\animtext0\f9\loch
Slower Ticks:}{\rtlch\afs22\ab0 \ltrch\hich\af9\loch\strike0\fs22\ulnone\ulc0\b0\animtext0\f9\loch
 Because gravity forces your frame of reference to use up speed dealing with the gravitational field, your speed through time decreases, making time pass more slowly. [}{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DjwQsKMh2v8" }{\fldrslt {\rtlch\afs22\ab0 \ltrch\hich\af9\loch\rtlch\alang255 \ltrch\lang255\langfe255\loch\cf9\lang255\ul\ulc0\dbch\langfe255\strike0\fs22\ulnone\ulc0\b0\animtext0\f9\loch
