GPS Satellites:}{\rtlch\afs22\ab0 \ltrch\hich\af9\loch\strike0\fs22\ulnone\ulc0\b0\animtext0\f9\loch
 Clocks on }{\rtlch\afs22\ab0 \ltrch\hich\af9\loch\strike0\fs22\ul\ulc0\b0\animtext0\f9\loch
GPS}{\rtlch\afs22\ab0 \ltrch\hich\af9\loch\strike0\fs22\ulnone\ulc0\b0\animtext0\f9\loch
 satellites orbit far above Earth. Because they experience less Earth gravity than we do on the ground, their clocks actually tick slightly faster (about 38 microseconds a day) and must be adjusted to keep navigation accurate.}{\hich\af5\loch\strike0\fs24\ulnone\ulc0\b0\animtext0\f5\loch
 }
