\par \pard\plain \s22\rtlch\af14\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1058\langfe2052\hich\af3\loch\ql\sl276\slmult1\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa140\ltrpar\cf0\f3\fs24\lang1058\kerning1\dbch\af12\langfe2052\loch{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af6 \ltrch\hich\af6\loch\f6\dbch\af6 \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls14 \li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi-283\tx0\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi-283\sb0\sa0\ltrpar{\hich\af5\loch\cs17\rtlch\ab \ltrch\loch\b\strike0\fs24\ulnone\ulc0\b\animtext0\f5\loch
Yes, it is the same ship (Identity by Form or Continuity):}{\hich\af5\loch\strike0\fs24\ulnone\ulc0\b0\animtext0\f5\loch
 If you replace parts one by one over time, the ship keeps its shape, function, name, and history. Legal and maritime traditions (like registry rules) treat it as the same vessel through endless repairs. Humans also view themselves this way, since our body cells constantly replace themselves while we remain "us".}
\par \pard\plain \s22\rtlch\af14\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1058\langfe2052\hich\af3\loch\ql\sl276\slmult1\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa140\ltrpar\cf0\f3\fs24\lang1058\kerning1\dbch\af12\langfe2052\loch{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af6 \ltrch\hich\af6\loch\f6\dbch\af6 \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls14 \li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi-283\tx0\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi-283\sb0\sa0\ltrpar{\hich\af5\loch\cs17\rtlch\ab \ltrch\loch\b\strike0\fs24\ulnone\ulc0\b\animtext0\f5\loch
No, it is a new ship (Identity by Matter):}{\hich\af5\loch\strike0\fs24\ulnone\ulc0\b0\animtext0\f5\loch
 If every original physical piece is gone, the actual matter has completely changed, making it numerically a brand-new object. This becomes even clearer if someone collected all your old discarded parts and rebuilt a second ship out of them\u8212\'97raising the question of which one is the "real" original. }
\par \pard\plain \s22\rtlch\af14\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1058\langfe2052\hich\af3\loch\ql\sl276\slmult1\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa140\ltrpar\cf0\f3\fs24\lang1058\kerning1\dbch\af12\langfe2052\loch\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0\sb0\sa0\ltrpar{\hich\af5\loch\strike0\fs24\ulnone\ulc0\b0\animtext0\f5\loch
If you like, we can explore how this paradox applies to }{\hich\af5\loch\cs17\rtlch\ab \ltrch\loch\b\strike0\fs24\ulnone\ulc0\b\animtext0\f5\loch
human identity and cells}{\hich\af5\loch\strike0\fs24\ulnone\ulc0\b0\animtext0\f5\loch
 or discuss }{\hich\af5\loch\cs17\rtlch\ab \ltrch\loch\b\strike0\fs24\ulnone\ulc0\b\animtext0\f5\loch
famous real-life examples}{\hich\af5\loch\strike0\fs24\ulnone\ulc0\b0\animtext0\f5\loch
 like the USS Constitution. Which would you prefer?}
