Obviously Python is the worst programming language}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af14\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1058\langfe2052\hich\af3\loch\ql\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f3\fs24\lang1058\kerning1\dbch\af12\langfe2052\loch\ql\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0\sb0\sa0\ltrpar{\rtlch\afs22\ab0 \ltrch\lang1033\hich\af9\loch\cs17\rtlch\ab \ltrch\loch\b\strike0\fs22\lang1033\ulnone\ulc0\b0\animtext0\f9\loch
Python is not the worst programming language; rather, it is one of the most widely used and versatile tools in the tech industry, despite its clear trade-offs in execution speed and strict type enforcement.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af14\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1058\langfe2052\hich\af3\loch\ql\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f3\fs24\lang1058\kerning1\dbch\af12\langfe2052\loch\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0\sb0\sa12\ltrpar{\rtlch\afs22\ab0 \ltrch\hich\af9\loch\strike0\fs22\ulnone\ulc0\b0\animtext0\f9\loch
Labeling Python as the worst is a misconception because language choice depends entirely on the task at hand. Below is an objective look at why Python is criticized, balanced with why it remains so dominant.}
